      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, 1863 saw William Quantrill's guerrillas seize a federal troop unit stationed in Plattsburg's courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plattsburg%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town grew beside the Little Platte River, which helped shape its early economy and transportation routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plattsburg%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By the 1830s, Plattsburg emerged as a railroad hub, linking Missouri's western frontier to national markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://plattsburgchamber.org/visit/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "After the 1836 Platte Purchase, Plattsburg hosted a federal land office that opened northern Missouri to new settlers.",
